257.         </h2>
258.         <div class="details hidden">
259.           <p>Cats have a wide range of vocalizations, each with its own meaning. Short meows are greetings, long meows express complaints or demands, and rapid-fire meows show excitement. Chirps and trills indicate friendly communication, while hisses and growls are clear warnings. Interestingly, cats rarely meow at each other — they reserve this behavior mainly for communicating with humans.</p>
260.         </div>
