268.           </button>
269.         </h2>
270.         <div class="details hidden">
271.           <p>The third eyelid, called the nictitating membrane, is a protective covering that helps keep a cat's eyes moist and clean. It sweeps across the eye to remove debris and protective secretions. If a cat's third eyelid becomes visible, it can be a sign of illness or stress, so it's worth consulting a veterinarian if you notice this change.</p>
