283.           <p>Cats possess an incredible righting reflex that allows them to rotate their bodies mid-air to land on their feet. This ability relies on their flexible spine, keen inner ear balance system, and visual processing. Starting from just a few feet, kittens gradually develop this skill, which becomes nearly automatic by adulthood. However, falls from extreme heights can still cause serious injury.</p>
